.TH T2TOP 1 "August 2026" "t2top 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
t2top \- hardware telemetry for Macs running Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B t2top
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B t2top
is a dependency-free terminal dashboard for Intel Macs with the Apple T2
security chip running Linux. It decodes the Apple SMC sensor wall (the
four-character keys exposed by the
.B applesmc
driver) into named temperatures, and shows fans with their controller
targets, battery health and cycle count, CPU per-core load and thermals,
dual-GPU telemetry, memory, disk, and network \(em all from /sys and /proc,
with no root, no configuration, and no libraries beyond libc.
.PP
On non-Mac hardware every panel degrades gracefully; the SMC wall simply
reports that no applesmc device exists.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-once
Render a single frame to stdout and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list
Plain-text dump of every discovered sensor, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-size " WxH"
Override the frame size (useful with \-\-once).
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " MS"
Sampling interval in milliseconds (default 500).
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-fahrenheit
Display temperatures in Fahrenheit.
.TP
.B \-\-256
Use 256-color output instead of 24-bit truecolor.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.TP
.B p
Pause sampling.
.TP
.B +/\-
Faster / slower sampling.
.TP
.B f
Toggle Celsius / Fahrenheit.
.SH FILES
Sensor sources include
.IR /sys/class/hwmon ,
.IR /sys/class/power_supply/BAT0 ,
.IR /proc/stat ,
and
.IR /proc/net/wireless .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sensors (1),
.BR btop (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Built for the t2linux community.
